### 3. Objective

Implement the Gear Selection page and the conditional Pots Details page for the Catch Record journey.

The user must be able to:

1. Select the gear used during the trip.
2. Submit the selection.
3. Continue directly to the next approved journey step when no selected gear requires pots details.
4. Continue to Pots Details when the selected gear requires that information.
5. Enter and submit the pots information shown in the supplied PNG.
6. Navigate backwards without losing valid saved data.

### 4. Background Context

Catch Recording is a frontend-only application with no backend or database.

All dummy reference data and journey data must use the repository's existing editable JSON object-file approach. Do not introduce a backend, database, remote API or hidden hard-coded data source.

This step follows Step 10, Departure and Return Ports. It precedes the next approved Catch Record journey step.

Reuse the shared header, centred menu, white middle logo dot, phase banner, Back link region, English/Cymraeg selector and footer with its thin grey top border. Do not redesign shared components.

