### 10. Journey and Branching Rules

Implement the approved equivalent of:

```text
Step 10 completed
  -> Gear Selection
     -> valid selection requiring pots information
        -> Pots Details
           -> next approved step
     -> valid selection not requiring pots information
        -> next approved step
```

If multiple selections are allowed and at least one selected option requires pots details, route to Pots Details.

The conditional rule must come from editable JSON configuration or an existing domain mapping, not visible labels and not template logic.

#### Back navigation

```text
Gear Selection
  -> explicit Step 10 Return Port route

Pots Details
  -> explicit Gear Selection route
```

If a user changes gear so pots details are no longer required, follow the approved state-cleanup rule defined during planning. Do not silently keep stale pots data if it could later appear in review or submission. Do not silently delete it unless the approved plan defines that behaviour.

### 11. Gear Selection Requirements

Implement exactly what the Gear Selection PNG shows.

The page must:

1. Load gear options from editable JSON.
2. Use the control type shown in the PNG.
3. Display options in the PNG order unless existing approved data explicitly defines the order.
4. Restore saved selections.
5. Validate required input.
6. Reject values not present in the approved data set.
7. Save valid selections using stable IDs rather than display labels where consistent with the existing model.
8. Route conditionally after successful submission.

If the PNG uses checkboxes, use the GOV.UK Checkboxes component and a page-heading legend. If the PNG uses radios, use GOV.UK Radios. Do not choose the component based on assumption.

### 12. Pots Details Requirements

Implement every visible field in the Pots Details PNG and no additional fields.

For each field, planning must record:

- Exact label
- Exact hint text
